From 403703d609123f4980dc8fd75fc51d85178048ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lateautumn233 <lateautumn233@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:28:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] k27: the single-volume layout: the root is the System
 volume of the Data container, launchd and APFS mount the rest

The root is the System volume DroidVMSystem of the Data store's APFS container, in the Data volume's volume group, as on a Mac.
launchd's mount-phase-1/2 (apfs_boot_util) mount VM, Preboot, Update, xART, Hardware and Data, and APFS stitches the firmlinks stored
on the System volume (docs/k27-real-disk-layout-plan.md). Verified: mount lists the seven volumes as on a Mac, / and the firmlinked
/Users, /Library, /private/var have the Data volume's device, '..' of a firmlink target is the source's parent, fseventsd, mds,
kernelmanagerd, WindowServer and loginwindow run.

native_owner_cache_prepare no longer mounts the SystemOS volume over the root: it checks the read-only verified APFS root and
publishes the boot manifest of the root alone (native_owner_publish_boot_manifest loses its cache volume).
native_owner_systemos_volume_uuid and native_verified_block_volume_device go with the mount.
---
 bsd/kern/kern_exec.c          | 118 ++++------------------------------
 iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp |  61 ++----------------
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 159 deletions(-)

